These positions are used to create lists of trait names corresponding to
the vegetative (\code{"veg"}), floral (\code{"flo"}), and fruit (\code{"fru"}) blocks.

Morphological values are converted to numeric format. During this process,
leading and trailing whitespace is removed, commas used as decimal
separators are converted to periods, empty strings are converted to \code{NA},
and infinite values are replaced with \code{NA}.

Rows and columns containing no morphological observations after conversion
are removed.

Each retained specimen receives a unique identifier in the form
\code{"ID0001"}, \code{"ID0002"}, and so forth. These identifiers are used as row
names in the returned morphometric matrix.

A colour is assigned to each taxon retained in the final matrix (i.e. after
all filtering steps). If \code{colors = NULL} (default), colours are drawn
automatically from the \code{viridis} palette. Alternatively, the user may
supply a named character vector (taxon name = colour) via \code{colors} to
define custom colours. This taxon-colour mapping is stored as the
\code{"taxon_colors"} attribute of the returned \code{analysis_data} object.
